"boycotting" != "avoiding".

I *avoid* rap and "jungle" music, because generally speaking, I don't
like them.  I don't *boycott* rap and "jungle" music.  If someone
came along and played me some rap or "jungle" that I actually liked,
I'd make an exception.  If I was *boycotting* rap and "jungle" music,
I'd refuse to buy any of it.

>> I'd wager that at this point most gamers haven't even
>> heard of these games.
>
>They've heard of them (or games like them), but still
>boycot them, because the find them boring.

In every colloquial usage I have ever encountered, "boycott" in relation
to a product specifically means refusing to use the product for some
reason other than the quality of the product - say, because the
manufacturers eat babies, or shag sheep, or sponsor people who firebomb
abortion clinics / run abortion clinics / publish homophobic pamphlets /
support gay rights.
